# Holding, owning and being in someone's care
#
# Three different things. Holding comes from events and is replayed. Nothing in the text transfers
#  title, so ownership isn't asserted.

@prefix iy:   <https://example.org/manichchilambu#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix crm:  <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/> .
@prefix crminf: <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/extensions/crminf/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix time: <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .

<https://example.org/manichchilambu/m06_custody> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "Holding, owning and being in someone's care" ; owl:imports <https://example.org/manichchilambu> .
# Closest standard term: crm:E10_Transfer_of_Custody

iy:Custody a owl:Class .
iy:Ownership a owl:Class .
iy:Care a owl:Class .

iy:holds a owl:ObjectProperty .
iy:owns a owl:ObjectProperty .
iy:inCareOf a owl:ObjectProperty .
